3d22689350466b5290b613a71b45074671b","position":"1788413794176457001-f272cc3d-635a-404c-8a28-0aca36bace77"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d3021eab7d29b25dcb00ec142ea1251c18bb2732251350203fafe4262792eae5","event_uuid":"62b355d3-5d4d-4650-ad02-ad25cad70cdd","position":{"commit_sha":"b461fedb826e1322d83a0b657781f0bf09293e87","position":"1788413800492802001-62b355d3-5d4d-4650-ad02-ad25cad70cdd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Research complete.\n\nEvidence: 2026 work supports selective, preservation-aware compression rather than blind shortening. “Valid ≠ Necessary” removed 31–53% of reasoning tokens while preserving accuracy; “When LLMs Over-Answer” reduced redundant answers 37% and non-core text 31%; “The Sleeping Agent” showed that an explicit preservation rule raised date retention from 3.05% to 62.39%; “Context Compression Cost” showed unchanged completion can hide extra state-retrieval work. Published 2025 studies add that uncertainty drives repetition/enumeration, long context hurts even with perfect retrieval, judges favor information mass, and adaptive budgets outperform tiny fixed caps.\n\nOSS convergence: OpenAI and Anthropic require every token to earn its place while protecting load-bearing context; OpenAI and Superpowers use progressive disclosure and cross-references; Anthropic recommends positive concise examples and qualitative rather than hard universal caps; wshobson statically scores exact repetition and imperative density but gives token efficiency only 9% weight; Claude Code scopes findings and uses confidence thresholds.\n\nRecommendation: require the minimum sufficient durable record, artifact-specific schemas, a keep/compress/delete pass, exact-fact preservation, and canonical links. Block only objective defects (substantial exact duplication, unsummarized transcript dumps, structurally empty updates); keep length, near-duplication, filler, paragraph length, alternative sprawl, and imperative density advisory. Evaluate completeness/relevance separately from length and measure downstream state reacquisition. No repository files changed.","timestamp":1788412934808409001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Deterministic-rule matrix (defaults to calibrate on the local corpus; protected spans are identifiers, paths, commands, dates, measurements, decisions, constraints, blockers, and exact error text):\n\n- Exact duplication — Signal: case/whitespace/list-marker-normalized prose unit of at least 8 words repeats. Threshold: flag any repeat; block if one unit occurs at least 3 times or duplicates comprise at least 15% of unprotected prose. Severity: advisory below the block threshold, blocking above it. Exempt: headings, table headers, checklist markers, code, logs, and versioned normative quotations.\n- Near/cross-history duplication — Signal: two units of at least 20 words, or a comment versus the description/last five comments, have token 5-shingle Jaccard at least 0.80. Threshold: one pair. Severity: advisory only. Exempt: test matrices or acceptance criteria with distinct protected facts; typed correction, resolution, or handoff records.\n- Transcript dump — Signal: at least 20 consecutive shell/log/JSON-like lines, or at least 2,000 transcript characters comprising over 25% of the artifact. Threshold: warn there; block above 50 lines or 4,000 characters when no at-most-100-word finding summary plus durable pointer/hash exists. Severity: advisory then blocking. Exempt: session logs and exact bug/security/incident evidence; those remain linked or attached rather than copied into the plan.\n- Structurally empty update — Signal: a comment has no non-empty Delta, Evidence, Decision, Blocker, or Next field and fewer than 8 content words with no identifier, metric, link, or command. Threshold: one comment. Severity: blocking. Exempt: machine-typed lifecycle events and monitoring heartbeats.\n- Filler/meta narration — Signal: configurable stock phrases such as “certainly,” “here is,” “it is important to note,” “as mentioned above,” or “in conclusion.” Threshold: at least 3 matches or over 2 per 100 prose words. Severity: advisory. Exempt: quotations and user-facing copy under review.\n- Paragraph/sentence sprawl — Signal: sentence over 45 words or prose paragraph over 120 words. Threshold: one occurrence. Severity: informational/advisory only. Exempt: code, exact errors, logs, legal text, and quotations.\n- Alternative/hedge sprawl — Signal: at least 3 Option/Alternative blocks or more than 3 hedge terms per 100 words. Threshold: one breach; for an executable plan, more than one mutually exclusive path without a Chosen or Blocked marker. Severity: advisory generally; blocking only for that unresolved executable-plan case. Exempt: ideas, ADRs, decision comparisons, and explicitly blocked discovery.\n- Imperative saturation — Signal: MUST/ALWAYS/NEVER directives exceed 1 per 10 nonblank lines or 15 total. Threshold: either. Severity: advisory only. Exempt: safety, compliance, or irreversible-operation constraints that state a reason.\n- Length envelope — Signal: size exceeds the versioned P95 for accepted artifacts in the same type/complexity bucket (minimum sample 200); fallback is 8,000 description characters, 600 plan words, or 150 comment words. Threshold: one breach. Severity: advisory only; a separate operational context-window limit may reject admission but does not prove verbosity. Exempt: marked exact evidence, security/incident/legal records, and generated specifications, with overflow linked.\n- Canonical-source copying — Signal: a linked local source and at least 100 copied words have 7-shingle containment of at least 0.50. Threshold: one block. Severity: advisory. Exempt: a version-pinned normative excerpt whose exact wording is itself evidence.\n\nApply a completeness floor before these checks; never auto-delete flagged prose or protected facts.","timestamp":1788413251986144001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788399027082733146,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nResearch how agents can write concise but complete ticket descriptions, plans, and comments. Use current evidence and examples from popular, actively maintained OSS prompt, skill, or Claude-plugin projects.\n\n## Plan\n- Review 2025-2026 primary research on controllable verbosity, compression, and evaluation.\n- Inspect maintained OSS agent-instruction repositories for concrete brevity patterns.\n- Synthesize agent guidance and deterministic bloat signals with false-positive safeguards.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Cite at least three 2025-2026 primary sources and four maintained OSS sources.\n- [x] Distinguish empirical evidence from practitioner convention.\n- [x] Give actionable agent guidance that preserves necessary facts.\n- [x] For each proposed check, state its computable signal, default threshold, severity, and exemption.\n- [x] Identify checks that must remain advisory because they cannot prove irrelevance.\n\n## Verification\nCross-check material claims against cited sources. Confirm the answer explicitly covers (1) agent-writing guidance and (2) deterministic rules for flagging bloated content.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"Read-only research and recommendation; no repository files will be changed.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f272cc3d-635a-404c-8a28-0aca36bace77","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["research","agents","writing-quality"],"ticket_id":"ee0c-1d25-1652-43c3","ticket_type":"task","title":"Research concise agent-authored ticket content","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a8f3fac2-694e-4b51-b145-defb2d18f793","0209d52d-2f28-4f30-95f2-f5ce136f4758","474ff35d-15f7-4176-b301-bd45c2663671","321f05d6-c7cb-40b9-bee7-087c89ba92e8","bd766c95-c6ab-49f8-a91b-c6cec332df17","a58ffa58-ad33-4bf0-a677-e5520fd37019","a0aca8dc-68d6-4dc0-8431-fbe917bf9022","8611fa38-ffc6-4181-98b7-b210f63ac03f","221970bb-cd1d-4c0a-ad67-a776176b301f","f272cc3d-635a-404c-8a28-0aca36bace77","62b355d3-5d4d-4650-ad02-ad25cad70cdd"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788416058286192001,"uuid":"fd8ffd33-7bfa-43be-80f0-1469c9dcf8e2"}